{"type":"message","id":"5c711064","parentId":"3e6e3ebb","timestamp":"2026-05-02T05:06:39.711Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_QP7lj0RpSxGqsd3LJEBSgCZ5|fc_00dfb72e201b8d6c0169f5865e98c0819196adcd0f5845d01e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"def greet(name, greeting=\"Hello\"):\n    return f\"{greeting}, {name}!\"\n\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n\n\ndef multiply(a, b):\n    return a * b\n\n\ndef fizzbuzz(n):\n    results = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if i % 15 == 0:\n            results.append(\"FizzBuzz\")\n        elif i % 3 == 0:\n            results.append(\"Fizz\")\n        elif i % 5 == 0:\n            results.append(\"Buzz\")\n        else:\n            results.append(str(i))\n    return results\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(greet(\"World\"))\n    print(add(2, 3))\n    print(fizzbuzz(20))\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777698399710}}
{"type":"message","id":"2d29138b","parentId":"5c711064","timestamp":"2026-05-02T05:06:48.144Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`hello.py` is a small demo script with a few simple utility functions.\n\nWhat it does overall:\n- Defines functions for greeting text, addition, multiplication, and FizzBuzz\n- When run directly, it:\n  - prints a greeting\n  - prints the result of `add(2, 3)`\n  - prints the FizzBuzz list from 1 to 20\n\nFunctions:\n\n- `greet(name, greeting=\"Hello\")`\n  - Builds and returns a greeting string\n  - `name` is the person/name to greet\n  - `greeting` defaults to `\"Hello\"` if not provided\n  - Example: `greet(\"World\")` → `\"Hello, World!\"`\n\n- `add(a, b)`\n  - Returns the sum of `a` and `b`\n  - Example: `add(2, 3)` → `5`\n\n- `multiply(a, b)`\n  - Returns the product of `a` and `b`\n  - Example: `multiply(2, 3)` → `6`\n  - Note: this function is defined but not used in the script’s main block\n\n- `fizzbuzz(n)`\n  - Returns a list of strings from `1` to `n`\n  - For each number:\n    - multiples of 15 → `\"FizzBuzz\"`\n    - multiples of 3 → `\"Fizz\"`\n    - multiples of 5 → `\"Buzz\"`\n    - otherwise → the number as a string\n  - Example: `fizzbuzz(5)` → `[\"1\", \"2\", \"Fizz\", \"4\", \"Buzz\"]`\n\nMain block:\n\n- `if __name__ == \"__main__\":`\n  - This runs only when the file is executed directly, not when imported\n  - It prints:\n    - `Hello, World!`\n    - `5`\n    - the FizzBuzz list for 1–20\n\nIf you want, I can also walk through the file line by line.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_00dfb72e201b8d6c0169f5866093908191a8aa14e048ab0d2c\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":758,"output":415,"cacheRead":10240,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11413,"cost":{"input":0.0018950000000000002,"output":0.0062250000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0025599999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01068}},"stopReason":"stop","t